  "intro": "Your client manufactures a mid-tier shampoo brand sold through major retailers. Volume has been steady, but input costs are climbing and the team is debating whether to push through a 25% list price increase. The concern is obvious: will the margin lift justify the customers you'll lose?",
  "facts": [
    "Current retail price: $490 per case (24 bottles)",
    "Current annual volume: 38,000 cases",
    "Variable cost per case: $338",
    "Fixed costs: $320,000 annually",
    "Price elasticity of demand: -0.5"
  ],
  "question": "What is the total profit impact of implementing the 25% price increase?",
  "guiding_nudge": "Start by figuring out the new price and how volume reacts, then compare profit before and after the change.",
  "framework_soundbite": "Price up means margin per unit rises but volume falls — the question is always which effect is bigger.",
